{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-76c9-3jph-rj3q","cve_id":"CVE-2025-7339","url":"https://api.github.com/advisories/GHSA-76c9-3jph-rj3q","html_url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-76c9-3jph-rj3q","summary":"on-headers is vulnerable to http response header manipulation","description":"### Impact\n\nA bug in on-headers versions `< 1.1.0` may result in response headers being inadvertently modified when an array is passed to `response.writeHead()`\n\n### Patches\n\nUsers should upgrade to `1.1.0`\n\n### Workarounds\n\nUses are encouraged to upgrade to `1.1.0`, but this issue can be worked around by passing an object to `response.writeHead()` rather than an array.","type":"reviewed","severity":"low","repository_advisory_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jshttp/on-headers/security-advisories/GHSA-76c9-3jph-rj3q","source_code_location":"https://github.com/jshttp/on-headers","identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-76c9-3jph-rj3q","type":"GHSA"},{"value":"CVE-2025-7339","type":"CVE"}],"references":["https://github.com/jshttp/on-headers/security/advisories/GHSA-76c9-3jph-rj3q","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-7339","https://github.com/expressjs/morgan/issues/315","https://github.com/jshttp/on-headers/issues/15","https://github.com/jshttp/on-headers/commit/c6e384908c9c6127d18831d16ab0bd96e1231867","https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-76c9-3jph-rj3q"],"published_at":"2025-07-17T21:17:19Z","updated_at":"2025-07-30T21:06:13Z","github_reviewed_at":"2025-07-17T21:17:19Z","nvd_published_at":"2025-07-17T16:15:35Z","withdrawn_at":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"on-headers"},"vulnerable_version_range":"< 1.1.0","first_patched_version":"1.1.0","vulnerable_functions":[]}],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N","score":3.4},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":null,"score":0.0}},"cwes":[{"cwe_id":"CWE-241","name":"Improper Handling of Unexpected Data Type"}],"credits":[{"user":{